From 0a63ed4dd88bfd3e0110b34291db45c5b2a900b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pypto-x-agent <agent@pypto-x.local>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 23:26:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 254/258] fix(execution): close verify-0043 R1-R3, refuse R4/R5
 partial rewrites

Round 2 of report schema v3, closing the coordinated-rewrite classes the
verify-0043 independent review found outside the boundary list:

* R1/R2/R3: the guarantee-detail family
  (guarantees/resolved.exactness_basis_detail, provider_accumulation,
  exactness_envelope) is now reconciled against the embedded invoked
  manifest document (portable qmatmul keeps the contract-derived
  exact_contract_bound envelope).  The report can no longer contradict its
  own embedded ground truth; the entry layer builds the family from the
  invoked provider so runtime fallback reports describe the executed path.
* R4: the vendor manifest thread counts (max_threads,
  threads.max_threads, threads.default_threads, library.default_threads)
  must agree with each other and be positive; the partial rewrite from
  ce3_max_threads.py is refused with
  report_provider_manifest_thread_facts_mismatch.  The fully coordinated
  probe-fact rewrite remains a registered residual (the count has no code
  constant).
* R5: resolution_decision.document gains the required selected_threads /
  selected_thread_mode fields; resolved_policy.resources.* and the selected
  candidate thread echo are reconciled against them, and without a runtime
  fallback they are re-derived from the embedded manifest plus the
  digest-checked requested policy.  The ce4 report-copy rewrite is refused;
  the runtime-fallback decision-body rewrite remains a registered residual
  together with resolution.plan_digest (plan payload not embedded).
* Tests: the two existing report-envelope shape tests are updated to the
  anchored semantics; nine new cases cover R1-R5, the fully coordinated
  registered rewrites and the invoked-path int8->portable fallback family.
* Docs: 0006 section 3.2/7.1 and the round-2 brief now carry the complete
  boundary list with the corrected thread-model wording.
